  "evidence": [
    {
      "id": "E1",
      "source": "ORG-01",
      "quote": "Org chart (2026): Hospital Executive over the Chairman Medical Board, the clinical departments, the Nursing Directorate, Pharmacy, Allied Health, Patient Safety and Quality, Clinical Informatics, Patient Services and Finance, HR and the Programme Office.",
      "speaker": "",
      "attribution": "document"
    },
    {
      "id": "E2",
      "source": "INT-01",
      "quote": "Every department has an unofficial clinical lead for IT. Surgery's is Professor Ho himself, and nothing gets configured for surgery without his say-so.",
      "speaker": "Chief Clinical Informatics Officer",
      "attribution": "testimony"
    },
    {
      "id": "E3",
      "source": "INT-01",
      "quote": "I do my design workshops with consultants, but I test the idea with Doreen's ward managers first. If they groan, I go back.",
      "speaker": "Chief Clinical Informatics Officer",
      "attribution": "testimony"
    },
    {
      "id": "E4",
      "source": "INT-01",
      "quote": "The residents will use anything that saves them a night's typing. The consultants decide whether it is allowed.",
      "speaker": "Chief Clinical Informatics Officer",
      "attribution": "claim"
    },
    {
      "id": "E5",
      "source": "INT-02",
      "quote": "My ward managers run the wards. The roster, the bed state, who gets the new tablets. If they say no, it is no.",
      "speaker": "Director of Nursing",
      "attribution": "testimony"
    },
    {
      "id": "E6",
      "source": "INT-02",
      "quote": "I will back this if the downtime procedures are written with the wards, not for them.",
      "speaker": "Director of Nursing",
      "attribution": "testimony"
    },
    {
      "id": "E7",
      "source": "INT-02",
      "quote": "I heard Surgery wants to keep paper drug charts for theatre.",
      "speaker": "Director of Nursing",
      "attribution": "hearsay"
    },
    {
      "id": "E8",
      "source": "INT-03",
      "quote": "E-prescribing removes the illegible chart, and my pharmacists want it. The risk is that the juniors click through the alerts.",
      "speaker": "Chief Pharmacist",
      "attribution": "testimony"
    },
    {
      "id": "E9",
      "source": "INT-03",
      "quote": "I speak to Aisha every week outside the programme meetings. That is where the drug library really gets decided.",
      "speaker": "Chief Pharmacist",
      "attribution": "testimony"
    },
    {
      "id": "E10",
      "source": "INT-03",
      "quote": "Professor Chua can stop anything at the Medical Board if the consultants complain loudly enough.",
      "speaker": "Chief Pharmacist",
      "attribution": "claim"
    },
    {
      "id": "E11",
      "source": "INT-04",
      "quote": "Amanda sponsors this and expects me to tell her within the day if Surgery pushes back.",
      "speaker": "Programme Director",
      "attribution": "testimony"
    },
    {
      "id": "E12",
      "source": "INT-04",
      "quote": "The funding comes in tranches from cluster headquarters and the Ministry reads our monthly report.",
      "speaker": "Programme Director",
      "attribution": "testimony"
    },
    {
      "id": "E13",
      "source": "INT-04",
      "quote": "The nurses' union branch asked to see the downtime plan. We have not yet sent it.",
      "speaker": "Programme Director",
      "attribution": "testimony"
    },
    {
      "id": "E14",
      "source": "INT-04",
